          "name": "Are solid-state hydrogen materials safe for agricultural use?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The silicon-hydrogen materials discussed here react mainly to release hydrogen, yielding SiO₂ / silicic acid and Mg–Ca products. No formal environmental safety assessment exists yet: pot and field trials plus ecotoxicology are required. MUQI has listed this as a priority topic for joint validation with SJTU; safety conclusions await completed testing, and this article makes no claims."
