          "name": "How does the hydrogen membrane maintain shelf stability without premature hydrogen outgassing?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Unlike liquid pre-soaked masks where dissolved hydrogen dissipates through packaging within hours, MUQI's hydrogen-infused membrane cloth stores hydrogen in a dry, chemically stable solid-state donor form (HI element) embedded via ion-plating. It remains inert during storage and activates exclusively upon contact with moisture (water, essence, or physiological fluids), generating fresh, high-concentration molecular hydrogen on demand."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can feminine hygiene manufacturers integrate hydrogen chips without retooling high-speed production lines?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Modern sanitary pad converting lines utilize automated rotary insertion modules originally engineered for anion or far-infrared functional chips. MUQI supplies the hydrogen-infused material pre-slit into standard chip dimensions (or 150cm master rolls), allowing seamless integration into the core absorption composite without line downtime or mechanical retooling."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What measurable metrics validate the hydrogen release performance of this fabric?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "In standard laboratory testing (1 sheet immersed in 50ml deionized water), dissolved molecular hydrogen exceeds 1300 ppb within 5 minutes. Continuous kinetic testing demonstrates sustained release curves of 1885 ppb at 5 min, 1774 ppb at 10 min, and 1648 ppb at 30 min, accompanied by a significant reduction in Oxidation-Reduction Potential (ORP) into negative millivolt territory."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What are the regulatory boundaries for marketing claims on hydrogen membrane products?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "B2B commercial copy must strictly distinguish between verified material characteristics and consumer efficacy. Brands may legally claim physical composition, moisture-triggered hydrogen release, measured ppb curves, softness, and breathability under cosmetic or hygiene standards (such as GB 15979-2024). Therapeutic, anti-inflammatory, or disease-curing claims are prohibited. Foundational molecular biology (such as Ohsawa et al., Nature Medicine 2007) is cited purely as academic literature, and medical dressings require statutory medical device registrations."
