            "text": "Solid-state hydrogen water media refers to passive, sintered inorganic ceramic-mineral composites—such as MUQI's Intelligent Controlled Release (ICR) ceramics—that generate 1,000-1,500 ppb of micro-nano dissolved molecular hydrogen upon contact with drinking or bath water without batteries, electrodes, or external power."
